Here is a MATLAB function that implements the described steps to denoise the input image using the Fourier transform and Gaussian filter:

```matlab
function denoised_image = denoise_image(I, sigma, filter_size)
    % Apply 2-D Fourier transform to the input image
    F = fft2(I);

    % Create Gaussian filter
    [X, Y] = meshgrid(-floor(filter_size/2):floor(filter_size/2), -floor(filter_size/2):floor(filter_size/2));
    G = exp(-(X.^2 + Y.^2) / (2 * sigma^2));
    G = G / sum(G(:));

    % Pad Gaussian filter to the size of the input image
    padded_G = zeros(size(I));
    padded_G(1:filter_size, 1:filter_size) = G;
    padded_G = circshift(padded_G, [-floor(filter_size/2), -floor(filter_size/2)]);

    % Apply Gaussian filter to the frequency domain image
    filtered_F = F .* fft2(padded_G);

    % Inverse-transform the filtered frequency domain image
    denoised_image = real(ifft2(filtered_F));
end
```

To use this function, you can call it with the input image matrix `I`, the standard deviation `sigma`, and the filter size `filter_size`. For example:

```matlab
% Load input image (assuming it is a grayscale image)
I = imread('input_image.png');

% Denoise the image using the provided function
sigma = 15;
filter_size = 30;
denoised_image = denoise_image(I, sigma, filter_size);

% Save the denoised image to a file
imwrite(denoised_image, 'denoised_image.png');
```

This code will apply the denoising process to the input image and save the denoised image to a file named 'denoised_image.png' in the current directory.

