\begin{pmatrix}
y_1 \\
y_2 \\
y_3 \\
\end{pmatrix}
=
\begin{pmatrix}
-1.5 \\
3.5 \\
10 \\
\end{pmatrix}

2. Backward substitution: Solve L^T x = y for x

L^T:
\begin{pmatrix}
2 & -0.5 & -0.5 \\
0 & 2.179 & -1.075 \\
0 & 0 & 2.015 \\
\end{pmatrix}
